### C1. Exact claims and core techniques of the two factoring papers

**1. Unconditional Las Vegas `L_N[1/3, 105]` factoring ([integer_factorization.txt](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/scratch/cogentic/integer_factorization.txt), Thm 1.1, §1.1 p. 2; §6 pp. 44–49).**
*Claim:* A fixed uniform Las Vegas multitape Turing machine (`Factor`/`SingleSplit`, Def 6.1, pp. 44–46) computes the AKS-certified prime factorization of every `N >= 2`, unconditionally and zero-error, in worst-case expected time `L_N[1/3, 105]` and deterministic workspace `L_N[1/3, 40]`.

*Fruitfulness (without `Conj F`):* Identical to our repo's sealed-root Dixon descent (`Theorem DD`, [notes/thmA_proof.md:300](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/thmA_proof.md#L300); [notes/mfU_theorem.md:35-49](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/mfU_theorem.md#L35-L49); [notes/fruit_results.md:132](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/fruit_results.md#L132)). In §6 `Step 3(a)–(b)` (p. 45), each trial draws `z_m` uniformly from `(Z/NZ)^*`, seals `z_m` until `Step 5`, exposes only `w_m = z_m^2 mod N`, and uses Lagrange–Gauss reduction to split `w_m ≡ x_1*y_1^{-1} (mod N)` into `2r_0 ≈ 3*Upsilon(N)` primes in `(Q_0/2, Q_0]` with `Q_0 ≈ L_N[2/3, 1/3]` (`Prop 2.3(2)`, p. 9 & App. A pp. 50–51 — our `Theorem S'` character-orthogonality count, [notes/hypD_results.md:203](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/hypD_results.md#L203)). Cofactors `x_1,y_1 <= sqrt(N)/2` and descent cofactors `<= N^{1/10}` are factored by strong-induction self-recursion (`Step 4`, pp. 48–49, matching `Lemma F_α` in [notes/mfU_theorem.md:806](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/mfU_theorem.md#L806)). Since descent, `F_2` elimination, and square roots inspect only `(w_m)` and independent coins, unsealing `Z = prod_{m in T_x} z_m` splits `N` with probability `1 - 2^{1-omega(N)} >= 1/2` (`Lemma 5.3`, p. 44).

*Rigorous `L[1/3]` relation supply + growing-degree `LV6'` (overcoming our `2/5`, `3/8`, and `ERH + Hyp AD + LV6'` in [notes/nested_results.md:485-499](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/nested_results.md#L485-L499)):*
1. *Two-field rational elimination (`Def 4.5`, §4 pp. 38–39):* Two odd-degree forms `f_1,f_2` (`d ≈ Upsilon/2`) share base `(g_0,g_1)` (`G ≈ L_N[2/3, 3]`). Depth 0 smooths `(a_0*g_1 - b_0*g_0)/q_0` directly to `B ≈ L_N[1/3, 18]` (`Lemma 4.3`, pp. 32–35). Deeper nodes (`>= 1`) cancel `a*g_1 - b*g_0` between `phi_1(gamma_1(a))` and `phi_2(gamma_2(a))`, requiring `f_iota(a)/q` and `f_{iota'}(a)` to be `y(j)`-smooth while keeping *both* algebraic sides active in `(V'_{A_1}/(K_1^*)^2) x (V'_{A_2}/(K_2^*)^2)`.
2. *Proportional Bernoulli acceptance + backward path telescoping (`Def 4.5`, `Lemma 4.6`, §4 pp. 38–40):* On ladder `Y_j = floor(exp((3/4)^j*l_Q))` (`Def 2.7(3)`, pp. 11–12), child cap `y(j) = Y_{min(j+2,J)}` bounds path depth by `r_max <= ceil(J/2) <= 0.65*ln ln N << d`. Instead of deterministic first-hit scans (which required simultaneous control of `> d+1` tree nodes in `Lemma OD`, [notes/nested_results.md:362-397](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/nested_results.md#L362-L397)), `DescentTree` accepts candidate `a` via `Bernoulli(p_acc)` proportional to smooth weight `X_a`. On locally good nodes (`Z_clean >= mu_t/2`), each `a in A_clean` has selection probability `<= (2/mu_t)*X_a`. Backward tower expectations along *one path at a time* cancel `mu_t^{-1}` (`sum_a (2/mu_t)*E[X_a | Y_{<t}] < 3`, p. 40 line 2159), conditioning on `r << d` ancestors and union-bounding over `<= log_2 N` children per step: `sum_{r<=r_max} (3*log_2 N)^r * 2*exp(-25*(ln ln N)^2) <= exp(-23*(ln ln N)^2)`.
3. *Mod-`N` discrete Laplace law (`Def 4.1`, `Lemma 4.2`, §4 pp. 28–32):* Coefficients follow `exp(-alpha_Lap*||c||_1)` on `L_N cap [-W,W]^{d+1}`, sampled via layer-cake boxes + `(3/4)`-LLL. Since `G^{d-J-4} > N`, any `R <= ceil(J/2)+3` evaluations decouple from `mod N` (`Lemma 4.2(3)`) and remain quasi-invariant under ancestor-vanishing polynomial shifts (`Lemma 4.4`, p. 36).
4. *Siegel-free hybrid weight (`Def 3.4`, `Lemma 3.5`, `Lemma 3.6(4)`, §3 pp. 18–28):* Replaces `1_{y_1-smooth}` by `(c_0*c_1*c_1*c_1)/(4u_0)!`, counting `n = m_1*p_1*...*p_{4u_0-1}` (`m_1 in (y_1/2,y_1]`, primes `p_i in (y_1/2,y_1]`). Small `gcd(z_0,m_AP) <= y_1^{3/10}` divides `m_1`; heavy low-conductor characters (`r <= y_1^{3/5}`) cancel on `m'_1` by Pólya–Vinogradov + truncated Brun sieve (`Lemma 3.3(2)`), avoiding Siegel zeros without Harper's preprint or Drappeau's Lemme 5; bad conductors `S_bad` (`|S_bad| <= L_N(1/3,1.48)`) are avoided by ancestor-resultant gcd pruning (`Lemma 3.6(4)`).
5. *Unconditional `LV6'` (`Lemmas 5.1–5.2`, §5 pp. 41–44):* Character primes `l <= x_ch ≈ 2^{L_N[1/3,8/15]}` beat Stark's `(2d)!` threshold (`ln x_ch >> c_St*(2d)!*ln|Delta| = L_N[1/3,1/3+o(1)]`, matching [notes/nested_results.md:447-453](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/nested_results.md#L447-L453) inside `B = L_N[1/3,18]`), leaving Landau–Page kernel `dim_{F_2}(E_1 x E_2) <= 2`. Pinning `f_iota(X,1) ≡ h_0(X) (mod 3)` irreducible of odd degree `d` makes 3 inert with `4 | (3^d+1)`, giving deterministic 3-adic Newton–Hensel roots (`Lemma 5.2`).

**2. Unconditional deterministic `L_N[3/4]` factoring and `L_p[1/2]` QNR ([deterministic_factoring_l34.txt](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/scratch/cogentic/deterministic_factoring_l34.txt), Thms 1.1–1.3, §1.2 p. 4).**
*Claims:* Unconditional deterministic algorithms: `A_factor` (Thm 1.1) splits composite `N >= 4` in `O(exp(3*(ln N)^{3/4})) = L_N[3/4,o(1)]`; `A_split` (Thm 1.2) splits non-prime-power `N` given even `M_tilde` divisible by `lcm_{p|N}(p-1)` in `exp(O((ln N)^{1/2}*ln ln N))*(ln M_tilde)*(ln N)^2`, and `A_qnr` finds a QNR mod prime `p` (`M_tilde = p-1`) in `L_p[1/2,O(1)]`; `A_exp` (Thm 1.3) outputs a divisor or such `M_tilde` (`ln M_tilde <= exp((ln N)^{0.65})`) in `O(exp(3*(ln N)^{3/4}))`.

*Part 2 (§§7–11, pp. 29–56) — `L[3/4]` without ERH by bypassing `DSR`:* `A_exp` implements our **Z-route** ([notes/detGRH_results.md:53-65](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/detGRH_results.md#L53-L65); [notes/zroute_results.md:22-30](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/zroute_results.md#L22-L30)): two totally real base-`m` fields annihilate prime valuations and real units via localization maps (`Lemma 7.4` & `TryPair` `Lemma 7.5`, pp. 32–37 — deterministic `Lemma XK-Z`, [notes/zroute_results.md:106-200](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/zroute_results.md#L106-L200), using root bisection, bordered-adjugate Gram matrices, and Legendre continued fractions) to certify `l^{E_l} ≡ 1 (mod N)`. It bypasses `DSR` and ERH via:
1. *Long-progression perturbation sweep (§8.2 pp. 38–39; `Lemma 9.4` pp. 48–50):* Answering `Observation FS` ([notes/detGRH_results.md:441](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/detGRH_results.md#L441)) and `Observation LV` ([notes/zroute_results.md:502](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/zroute_results.md#L502)), it sets `d ≈ (ln N)^{0.30}`, `m = ceil(N^{1/d}) ≈ exp((ln N)^{0.70})`, `A ≈ 2^{(ln N)^{0.44}}`, `B ≈ 2^{(ln N)^{0.36}}`, and sweeps `P_0*l*(X-m)*(u_0+u_1*X)` over `(u,v) in B_U^2` with `U ≈ 2^{(ln N)^{0.75}} >> m`. Because Gaussian width exceeds modulus `P_0*l*|a-m| ≈ exp((ln N)^{0.70})`, Landau–Page cosine repulsion (`Lemma 9.2(3)`, pp. 46–47), Montgomery zero-density (`Prop 9.3`, pp. 47–48), and stopping-time Gram peeling (`Prop 10.1`, pp. 51–55) guarantee a witness in `B_U^2` for `(1/2-o(1))*B/ln B` primes `l in (B/2,B]` (`f_1 mod l` split, `f_2 mod l` root-free, `Lemma 8.1`, p. 37). Exhaustive search takes `2^{(4+o(1))*(ln N)^{3/4}} = O(exp(3*(ln N)^{3/4}))` (`4*ln 2 ≈ 2.773 < 3`, §11.2 p. 56).
2. *Subgroup-index saturation (`Lemma 11.1`, p. 55):* Certifying `l^{M_*} ≡ 1 (mod N)` on `>= B/(6*ln B)` primes keeps `k`-products (`k = floor(ln(p_j-1)/ln B)`) distinct below `p_j`, bounding `[F_{p_j}^* : G] < K_idx ≈ exp(O((ln N)^{0.64}*ln ln N))`; multiplying `M_*` by prime powers `<= K_idx` covers `p_j-1` without ERH.

*Part 1 (§§2–6, pp. 7–29) — `algSplit` and `L_p[1/2]` QNRs:* If Miller's 2-Sylow test (`Lemma 3.1`, pp. 13–15) fails on `-1,q_1,...,q_K` (`K ≈ (ln q)^{1/2}`), their odd-part powers lie in one cyclic 2-group mod `N`, yielding compatible roots `s_l^2 ≡ d_l (mod N)` across `2^K-1` quadratic fields `F_l` and biquadratic composita `E_{l_1,l_2}`. `Lemma 4.2` (pp. 15–20) enumerates modular images of unit and short principal-ideal generators via Gauss cycles and relative-norm + 4D weighted-LLL walks. If active character `chi(z) = (z/q)` equals `+1` on `[1,Y]` and those generators, `chi o phi_{F,q}` extends cocycle-freely to ideal characters `chi^*_l,chi^*_E` (`Lemma 5.1`, pp. 20–22). For `r > Y` with `chi(r) = +1` splitting in `F_{l_1},F_{l_2}`, `r*O_E = Q_{++}Q_{+-}Q_{-+}Q_{--}` forces `chi^*_{l_1}(p_{l_1})*chi^*_{l_2}(p_{l_2})*chi^*_{l_1+l_2}(p_{l_1+l_2}) = chi^*_E(Q_{++})^2*chi(r) = +1` (p. 21 line 1408). That `F_2`-linearity gives `(b_l(n))_l` a nonnegative Walsh–Hadamard transform at every `n`, forcing `max_l S^{cop}_l(q^{1/3}) > (1/2)*q^{1/3}*exp(-L_m^{1/2})` (`Lemma 6.4`, pp. 27–28) against a uniform 16th-moment Burgess bound `<< 4^K*D_l^3*q^{1/3-1/4000}` (`Lemma 6.3`, pp. 23–26).

### C2. Repo comparison and barrier audit

* **Superseded (if correct):** `Theorem A` ([notes/thmA_proof.md:91](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/thmA_proof.md#L91)), `Theorem U-MF` (`L[2/5]`, [notes/mfU_theorem.md:18](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/mfU_theorem.md#L18)), `Theorem 2L-final`/`2L-MF` (`L[3/8]`, [notes/thmAB_results.md:40-42](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/thmAB_results.md#L40-L42); [notes/audit2L_audit.md:36](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/audit2L_audit.md#L36); [STATUS.md:374](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/STATUS.md#L374)), and conditional `Theorem NR` ([notes/nested_results.md:496](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/nested_results.md#L496)) are superseded by Paper 1's unconditional `L_N[1/3, 105]`. Worst-case deterministic factoring improves from `N^{1/5+o(1)}` ([README.md:45](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/README.md#L45)) to `L_N[3/4]` (Paper 2 Thm 1.1), and order-multiple splitting (`Prop PIN`, [notes/zroute_results.md:278](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/zroute_results.md#L278)) drops ERH in `L_N[1/2]*ln M_tilde` (Paper 2 Thm 1.2).
* **Not superseded / consistent:** `Theorem AV` ([notes/avgtime_results.md:273](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/avgtime_results.md#L273)) still beats Paper 2 on *average* deterministic time (`L_X[1/2,sqrt(2)]` vs `L_N[3/4]`). `detGRH`/`zroute` at `L[1/2]` and `DSR_{1/2}` stay open. `Theorem DL`/`DL25` (`L_p[2/5]` in `F_p^*`, [notes/dlog_results.md:386](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/dlog_results.md#L386); [notes/dlog25_results.md:24](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/dlog25_results.md#L24)) is not superseded by Paper 3 ([discrete_logarithm.txt](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/scratch/cogentic/discrete_logarithm.txt) Thm 1.2 p. 2 requires `ln p <= (ln ln ln n)^2/4`), though Paper 1 + `Prop XK` should lift `F_p^*` DLP to `L_p[1/3]`. Our `lowerbound` theorem (`alpha >= 1/3`, `c >= 1.2114`/`1.5263`, [notes/lowerbound_results.md:42-67](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/lowerbound_results.md#L42-L67)) and GRH assessments ([notes/grhremark_results.md:17](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/grhremark_results.md#L17); [notes/masullo_results.md:13-14](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/masullo_results.md#L13-L14)) stand intact (`c = 105 >> 1.5263`).
* **No proved repo barrier is contradicted:**
  * `dsr` `Thm SB`, `Thm FN`, `Prop BOX-∞` ([BARRIERS.md:36](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/BARRIERS.md#L36); [notes/dsr_results.md:132,244,304](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/dsr_results.md#L132)): Rule out black-box walks, small Fourier-norm certificates on `S_can`/`S_Gauss`, and short multipliers for *prescribed* targets like `2^H`. Paper 2 never targets `2^H`: it scans `L[3/4]` polynomial perturbations wider than modulus `exp((ln N)^{0.70})` and saturates index from whichever `>= B/(6*ln B)` primes succeed (explicitly outside `BOX-∞`/`FN`, [notes/dsr_results.md:271-272,342](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/dsr_results.md#L271-L272)).
  * `nested` `Prop R2`, `Lemma OD`, `Prop BT` ([notes/nested_results.md:332,362,401](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/nested_results.md#L332)) & `escapeR2` `Lemma TI`/`Cor EX`/`Prop R3` ([notes/escapeR2_results.md:154,183,437](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/escapeR2_results.md#L154)): Paper 1 keeps algebraic children (`Prop R2`), closes each side's ideals in-field while certifying squares in *both* `K_1,K_2` (`Lemma TI`/`Cor EX` respected — rational cofactors cancel, not algebraic ideals), and builds `<= exp((ln ln N)^2) >> d`-node trees (outside `Prop R3`'s `kappa*(d-2)` budget) whose *single paths* have `r <= 0.65*ln ln N << d` nodes. Bernoulli acceptance + path telescoping (`Lemma 4.6`) conditions on one `r`-node path at a time, bypassing `Lemma OD` (a method barrier, not an impossibility, [notes/nested_results.md:389-390](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/nested_results.md#L389-L390)) and `Prop BT`.
  * `fruit` (`Prop SR`, `Prop IV-LV`, [notes/fruit_results.md:52-55](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/fruit_results.md#L52-L55)) & `rkrank` ([notes/rkrank_results.md:28-53](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/rkrank_results.md#L28-L53)): Pure-NFS `Conj F` is untouched; Paper 1 uses pure sealed-root Dixon descent (`Lemma 5.3`), avoiding `rkrank` and `Prop IV-LV`.

### C3. Repurposing toward `alpha < 1/3`

**None of the three papers helps achieve `alpha < 1/3`:**
* **Paper 1 stays inside all three `lowerbound` walls ([notes/lowerbound_results.md:109-120](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/lowerbound_results.md#L109-L120); [STATUS.md:382-387](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/STATUS.md#L382-L387)):** `w_tilde` has Dickman-scale density `(4u_0*ln y_1)^{-4u_0}` (`H` unbroken; Bernoulli telescoping fixes proof conditioning, not smoothness scarcity); rank-2 binary forms with `N | f_iota(g_0,g_1)` obey the proved `c >= 1.5263` profile (`LP_exc^rel` unbroken, [notes/lowerbound_results.md:67](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/lowerbound_results.md#L67)); and `R_tot = D_row+3` fresh trees have zero cross-row reuse (`R` unbroken).
* **Paper 2's biquadratic Walsh–Hadamard linearity (`Lemma 3.1(3)`, `Lemma 5.1`):** Realizes `V_4` `TIED-PARITY` ([notes/escapeR2_results.md:213-233](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/escapeR2_results.md#L213-L233)), but building compatible roots `s_l^2 ≡ d_l (mod N)` requires `M_tilde` (already factoring-equivalent in `L[1/2]`), and `D_l <= 4*P_K ≈ K^K` caps `K` at `L[1/2]`.
* **Paper 3 vs characteristic obstruction ([notes/equivtarget_results.md:31-44](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/equivtarget_results.md#L31-L44)):** Every ring map `Z/NZ -> A` into an `F_p`-algebra (`gcd(N,p)=1`) is zero. Paper 3's linearized pencils (§1.2 p. 4; `Lemma 3.3` p. 12) require characteristic-`p` Frobenius additivity `(x+y)^{q_0} = x^{q_0}+y^{q_0}` (`AGL_N(F_{q_0})` monodromy) and `phi_q(I_0) = I_0 + Q`, absent over `Z`.

### C4. Credibility read, constants, Lean claim, and referee priorities

* **Internal consistency & `(105, 40)`:** Both factoring `.txt` papers are non-circular, stub-free, and numerically tight, with dependency-ordered rational schedules and genuine fixes for subtle traps (skewness excision, absorbing `p | c_{iota,d}` into `V'_{A_iota}`, clearing index primes via `f'_iota(theta_iota)^2` in [notes/lv6_results.md:114](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/lv6_results.md#L114) style, and semiprime `q = p_1*p_2` when `e_1 = ... = e_s`). Constants `(105, 40)` are transparent: `beta = 18` (`B ≈ L_N[1/3,18]`) lets `f'' >= L_N[1/3,10.6]` beat `H_0*L_N[1/3,4.01] <= L_N[1/3,8.25]` in `Lemma 3.6(4)` (p. 28); dense `F_2` elimination on `R_tot ≈ L_N[1/3,18]` rows takes space `O(R_tot^2) <= L_N[1/3,37.4] < 40` (p. 47); and `M_cap ≈ L_N[1/3,21.15]` root splits recursively factor `x_1,y_1 <= sqrt(N)/2`, inflating time to `21.15/(1-2^{-1/3}) ≈ 102.52 < 105` (p. 49 — our `Theorem NR` recursion formula, [notes/nested_results.md:498](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/nested_results.md#L498)).
* **Lean 4 claim:** Highly implausible until code is released. None of the `.txt` papers mentions Lean; only the READMEs promise a "companion submission" in Mathlib-only `Lean 4 (v4.35.0)` ([integer_factorization_README.md:24](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/scratch/cogentic/integer_factorization_README.md#L24)) vs `v4.33.0` ([deterministic_factoring_l34_README.md:37](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/scratch/cogentic/deterministic_factoring_l34_README.md#L37)) without custom axioms. Mathlib lacks AKS, effective Chebotarev, Stark's lemma, Landau–Page repulsion, Montgomery zero-density, and multitape TM complexity libraries (compare [notes/grhremark_results.md:78-82](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/grhremark_results.md#L78-L82)).
* **Top 3 referee checkpoints:**
  1. **Paper 1, §4 `Lemma 4.6` (pp. 39–40) + `Lemma 4.4(1)` (pp. 35–37):** Verify backward path telescoping measurability — charging filter gap `A_alg \ A_clean` at node `r`, `P_Lap^{x 2}` slice conditioning on `(f_1(a_s^*),f_2(a_s^*))_{s<t}` (`p_1 ∤ f_2(a_0^*)` at `t=0`, line 2133), and unbiasedness of capped rejection/Bernoulli draws (`Def 4.5`, p. 38).
  2. **Paper 1, §3 `Lemma 3.5(4)(a)` & `Lemma 3.6(4)` (pp. 21–28):** Verify `(g_AP*phi(m'))^{-1}` cancellation when absorbing `gcd(z_0,m_AP) <= y_1^{3/10}` into `m_1` (compare [notes/ldbound_results.md:57](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/ldbound_results.md#L57), [notes/pcest_results.md:46](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/pcest_results.md#L46)), and the prime-power partition (`lines 1476–1496`) ruling out `f_flat <= H_0` for `f in S_bad`.
  3. **Paper 2, §6 `Lemma 6.3` (pp. 23–26) & §§9–10 `Prop 9.3` + `Prop 10.1` (pp. 47–55):** Check semiprime `Type III` 16th-moment fiber bounds for small `p_1` (`lines 1643–1646`), greedy factorization `n = m_1*m_2*m_3` (`Prop 9.3`, p. 48 lines 2924–2949), and stopping-time peeling preserving `H^*_true > 0` (`Prop 10.1(2)`, pp. 54–55).
